// Title: Drop Binaries Into Spool Drivers Color Folder
// Sigma ID: ce7066a6-508a-42d3-995b-2952c65dc2ce
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-07-28 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth
// Description: Detects the creation of suspcious binary files inside the
//   "\windows\system32\spool\drivers\color\" as seen in the blog referenced below
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2022/07/27/untangling-knotweed-european-private-sector-offensive-actor-using-0-day-exploits/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_susp_spool_drivers_color_drop.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\System32\\spool\\drivers\\color\\" and (FolderPath endswith ".dll" or FolderPath endswith ".exe" or FolderPath endswith ".sys")
